# Billing

A [promotion](/handbook/promotions) is written into the membership amount. The invoice shows it as its own line. It does not apply to the annual fee, shares, or the new-member fee.

CSA Admin aims to automate most tasks related to billing ([memberships](#memberships)<% if Current.org.feature?("shares") %>, [share capital](#share-capital)<% end %>, [payment processing](#payments))<% if Current.org.feature?("activity") %>, but some aspects such as billing for [uncompleted <%= activities_human_name %>](#activity) must be done manually<% end %>.

## Invoice types {#invoice-types}

CSA Admin handles several types of invoices:

| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Membership** | Main subscription billing (<%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %>, <%= BasketComplement.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %>, depot, delivery cycle). [Automatically generated](#memberships). |
<% if Current.org.feature?("annual_fee") %>| **Annual fee** | Included in the first membership invoice, or [billed separately](#annual-fee) for [support members](/handbook/members#statuses). |
<% end %><% if Current.org.feature?("shares") %>| **Share capital** | For organizations requiring [share ownership](#share-capital). Automatically generated when shares are missing. |
<% end %><% if Current.org.feature?("activity") %>| **<%= activities_human_name %>** | Billing for [uncompleted participations](#activity). Triggered manually or in group. |
<% end %><% if Current.org.feature?("shop") %>| **Shop order** | Invoice for [shop](/handbook/shop) orders. Can be automatic or manual. |
<% end %><% if Current.org.feature?("new_member_fee") %>| **New member fee** | One-time fee charged to new members, if the feature is enabled. |
<% end %>| **Other** | [Free-form invoices](#manual-invoice) for miscellaneous items or services. |

### Canceling invoices {#canceling-invoices}

To cancel an invoice for a membership or participation, first cancel or delete any more recent invoices for the same membership or participation. The **Cancel** button on earlier invoices remains disabled until then.

## Invoice settings {#invoice-settings}

Invoice settings define the bank and organization details displayed on invoice PDFs. Configure your bank account, the creditor address, optional invoice logos, and the information/footer text shown on invoices from [the invoice settings](/settings#invoice).

In SEPA countries, the invoice document name can also be customized per language when the SEPA feature is enabled.

<!-- country:CH -->
## QR-Invoices {#qr-invoices}

CSA Admin generates QR-invoices with reference numbers (PDF) and sends them to all emails of the concerned member.

### QR-IBAN {#qr-iban}

To generate these invoices, you need a **QR-IBAN** from your bank. This is a special IBAN (starting with CH and containing 30 or 31 as the bank clearing number) that is different from your regular bank account IBAN. Only the QR-IBAN allows generating Swiss QR-invoices with reference numbers — a normal IBAN is not supported for this purpose.

You can request a QR-IBAN from your bank and then enter it in [your invoice settings](/settings#invoice).

> If you're unsure whether you already have a QR-IBAN, try entering it in [your invoice settings](/settings#invoice) — the system will validate its format and reject it if it's not a valid QR-IBAN. If you don't have one, request it from your bank.
<!-- /country:CH -->

## Memberships {#memberships}

Membership billing is completely automated by the system. You can define in [the settings (Automatic billing)](/settings#billing) the day of the week when the system will review all memberships and automatically create and send necessary invoices.

It is therefore crucial that each membership configuration is up to date so that invoices are correct.

### Recurring automatic billing {#recurring-billing}

Recurring billing is the mechanism that handles membership invoicing. It must be enabled for any membership invoice to be created; without it, no membership invoices are generated or sent at all.

#### How to enable it

In [the settings (Automatic billing)](/settings#billing), choose the **day of the week** on which the system should run. Every week on that day, the system reviews all members and creates invoices when due. Invoices created this way are **automatically sent** by email.

By default, invoices that are already considered paid/closed when created are not sent automatically. You can change this with the "Send closed invoices" setting.

> It is advisable to choose a day other than the delivery day. This way, any membership or basket changes made on the delivery day are reflected in the invoice generated in the following days, rather than being invoiced prematurely the same day or waiting a full week.

An IBAN in [the invoice settings](/settings#invoice) is not enough. Without a weekday in [Automatic billing](/settings#billing), no membership invoices are created and [Invoice now](#bill-now) stays hidden. Overdue reminders follow [automatic payment import](#automatic_payments_processing), not this weekday.

### Which button? {#billing-cookbook}

- **Future** memberships (start date still ahead): [Invoice all in advance](#future_billing) from the membership page or from [the Future scope](/memberships?scope=future). That button is not on ongoing memberships.
- **Ongoing** memberships: wait for the billing weekday, or use [Invoice now](#bill-now) on the member or membership page when it is shown.
- **Invoice now** creates the same invoice as the automatic run, but **unsent**. Open the PDF, then Send. Automatic billing sends on the weekday.

<%= BasketComplement.model_name.human(count: 2) %> are on the membership invoice. They are not billed separately. [<%= Member.human_attribute_name(:salary_basket) %>](/handbook/members#salary-basket) zeroes those complements too.

#### Payment intervals {#billing-year-divisions}

Each membership has a **payment interval** (also called billing year division) that determines how many invoices are generated over the fiscal year. The available intervals are configured in [the settings](/settings#billing) and offered to members during registration or renewal.

Available intervals: Annual (1), Semi-annual (2), Four-monthly (3), Quarterly (4), Monthly (12).

The invoice amount is calculated as: **total membership amount ÷ number of remaining intervals**. For example, for a 1000 membership paid quarterly, each invoice will be 250.

### When is the first invoice sent? {#first-invoice-timing}

By default, the first invoice is sent on the billing day following the **first <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %> delivery**. With [trial <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %>](#trial-baskets), that date is the last trial delivery, not the first <%= Basket.model_name.human.downcase %>. No invoice is generated before that delivery.

This behavior can be changed in [the settings](/settings#billing) by disabling "Bill memberships only after their first delivery". When disabled, billing starts from the **membership start date**, even before any delivery. With a trial still running, it then waits for the first non-trial delivery.

### When does billing end? {#billing-end}

By default, billing extends until the **membership end date**, covering the full fiscal year even if there are no deliveries in the last months.

This can be changed in [the settings](/settings#billing) by enabling "Bill memberships until their last delivery only". When enabled, billing only covers up to the month of the last delivery. This is useful when the last months of the fiscal year have no deliveries.

#### Detailed logic

Each billing day, the system checks every member and determines whether an invoice is due:

1. The fiscal year is divided into periods based on the payment interval (e.g. quarterly = 4 periods of 3 months).
2. If the **current period has already been billed**, the next invoice is scheduled for the beginning of the next period. If the membership is already over-invoiced, it is scheduled for the next billing day instead, so the last invoice can be canceled and recreated.
3. If the membership **has already ended** (end date today or earlier), remaining periods no longer apply. Any remainder is billed on the next billing day.
4. If the **current period has not been billed yet**, the invoice is created on the next billing day, respecting the "first delivery" or "membership start" setting described above.
5. If the calculated next invoice date falls **after the fiscal year end**, no further invoice is generated for this year.

The invoice is always created on the configured day of the week. If an invoice becomes due on a different day (e.g. a new period starts on a Wednesday but billing day is Monday), it will be created the following Monday.

#### Next invoice date

From a member's or membership's page, the "Billing" section (right column) displays the **next invoice date**. This shows when the next automatic invoice will be created and sent.

This date updates dynamically: once an invoice is sent, it moves to the next scheduled date.

### Invoice now {#bill-now}

In some cases, for example after a change in membership configuration, you may want to create an invoice immediately rather than waiting for the next billing day. To do this, click on the "Invoice now" button in the "Billing" section (right column) of the member's or membership's page.

The invoice will be created but **not sent**. You can consult the PDF and send it manually using the "Send" button on its page. This is useful if you're in contact with a member and want to quickly rectify an invoice or verify the result of a configuration change.

> The "Invoice now" button produces the exact same invoice as the automatic system would, the only difference is that it's not sent automatically, giving you a chance to review it first.

The button is missing when recurring billing has no weekday, the IBAN is missing, the member is a [<%= Member.human_attribute_name(:salary_basket).downcase %>](/handbook/members#salary-basket), or nothing remains to bill. It also stays hidden while the current period is already billed, unless the membership has already ended and a remainder is still due.

### Invoice all in advance {#future_billing}

It is possible to invoice an upcoming subscription in advance, with a start date in the future, whether it is in the current fiscal year or the next fiscal year. Subscriptions invoiced in this way are fully invoiced at once, regardless of the payment interval configured for the subscription.

Advance invoicing can be done from the page of a future subscription by clicking on the "Invoice all in advance" button in the "Billing" section (right column). That invoice is created **unsent**, like [Invoice now](#bill-now). From [the subscriptions page](/memberships?scope=future&q[during_year]=<%= Current.fy_year + 1 %>), the same button under the filters invoices several future subscriptions at once and **sends** those invoices. Filter by fiscal year, and by payment interval (e.g. "Annual") if you want a narrower set.

> The annual fee corresponding to the fiscal year of the subscription is automatically included in the invoice.

### Price change {#price-change}

If a membership configuration (dates, <%= BasketSize.model_name.human.downcase %>, ...) is modified, several cases are possible:

- A future invoice still needs to be sent (it's the middle of the year and the member is billed each quarter) and the remaining amount is still positive; in this case, the price change (positive or negative) will simply be applied to the next invoice.
- The last invoice has already been sent, or the membership is already over-invoiced (no remaining positive invoice is possible), there are then 2 possibilities:
  - The price change is positive, a new invoice (with a higher amount) will simply be created on the next billing day to bill the missing amount.
  - If the price change is negative, the membership's most recent invoice or invoices are automatically canceled. A new invoice with the lower amount is created on the next billing day. If a canceled invoice was already paid, the new invoice is automatically closed and the member has a positive balance. To record a refund, [create a negative payment](/payments/new).

Shortening a membership end date, including with the **Stop** action, follows the same rule: future deliveries are removed, the membership amount is recalculated, and the difference is handled on the next billing day.

<% if Current.org.feature?("annual_fee") %>
### Annual fee {#annual-fee}

When the annual fee feature is enabled, the organization's default annual fee is defined in [the annual fee settings](/settings#annual_fee). Each member inherits this default when created, but it can be overridden individually from their profile (edit page, "Billing" section). If the "support members only" setting is enabled, active members do not automatically inherit the organization default annual fee; the default remains intended for support members unless set manually.

When enabled, the annual fee is automatically included in the **first invoice** of the membership. If the member doesn't have a membership ([support](/handbook/members#statuses)), a specific annual fee invoice is automatically created at the beginning of the fiscal year.

If you change the organization's default annual fee, all members still set to the previous value are automatically updated to the new one.
<% end %>

### Trial <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %> {#trial-baskets}

If a number of trial <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %> is defined in [the billing settings](/settings#billing), members can cancel the membership themselves from their account until the day before the first non-trial delivery. The membership then ends on the last trial delivery. To cancel immediately, an admin must do it.

By default, the first membership invoice is created on the billing day after the **last trial** delivery. That can still be while the member can cancel. If you disable "Bill memberships only after their first delivery", billing waits for the first **non-trial** delivery instead.

If the membership is canceled during the trial, only the delivered <%= Basket.model_name.human(count: 2).downcase %> are billed on the next billing day.<% if Current.org.feature?("annual_fee") %> The annual fee is not billed unless the member chooses to pay it.<% end %>

<% if Current.org.feature?("shares") %>[Share capital](#share-capital) invoices wait until the trial is over: missing shares are billed then. <% end %>Cancel or Stop the membership before a tacit renew, or the next fiscal year is created and billed.

### <%= Member.human_attribute_name(:salary_basket) %>

Members flagged as "[<%= Member.human_attribute_name(:salary_basket).downcase %>](/handbook/members#salary-basket)" are completely excluded from billing. Their membership still exists for delivery tracking, but all prices are zeroed out and no membership invoices are generated.

