## Uncompleted <%= activities_human_name %> {#activity}

Each organization has a different billing policy for uncompleted <%= activities_human_name.downcase %>, some bill them, others don't.
CSA Admin allows you to bill uncompleted <%= activities_human_name.downcase %> individually or in groups.

### Defining members to bill

The dashboard displays the total number of uncompleted <%= activities_human_name.downcase %>. For more detail, export the membership CSV for the relevant fiscal year from [the memberships page](/memberships). Use the "<%= activities_human_name %> missing" column to identify members to bill, then adjust the number requested for each member in their membership if necessary (field: "<%= activities_human_name %> (full year)").

### Individual billing

Either using the "Bill" button from a rejected participation page or from [the new invoice creation page](/invoices/new). Simply enter the number of <%= activities_human_name.downcase %> to bill and click on the "Create Invoice" button.

Don't forget to send the invoice, it's not sent automatically so you can check it.

### Group billing

From [the participations page](/activity_participations), below the filters, a "Billing" section allows you to bill all missing participations for a specific year in one click. ✨

Invoices are automatically sent here.

### Content of [the "New invoice" email](/mail_templates/invoice_created) {#activity-email}

It's possible to add specific text in the ["New invoice" email template](/mail_templates/invoice_created) for <%= activities_human_name.downcase %> invoices using [Liquid syntax](https://shopify.github.io/liquid) as follows:

~~~ liquid
{% case invoice.entity_type %}
  {% when 'ActivityParticipation' %}
    <p>My special text!</p>
  {% else %}
    <p>My standard text.</p>
{% endcase %}
~~~
<% end %>

## Manual invoice (Other) {#manual-invoice}

Use a manual invoice to bill miscellaneous items or services, such as fabric bags for new members. [Create a new invoice](/invoices/new), then add the items under the "Other" tab. After reviewing the PDF, send the invoice from its page.

> Note: Do not use "Other" invoices for memberships, share capital, or <%= activities_human_name.downcase %>; the system does not include them in those calculations.
>
> Recurring billing does not run on a closed past fiscal year membership. For that year, cancel the last invoice if needed and create an Other invoice, or [ask support](/support).

<% if Current.org.feature?("vat") %>
## VAT {#vat}

If your organization is subject to VAT, enable the VAT feature and configure your VAT number and rates in [the VAT settings](/settings#vat). Separate rates can be defined for membership invoices, <%= activities_human_name.downcase %> invoices, and shop order invoices. For "Other" and "New member fee" invoices, the VAT rate is set manually on each invoice.

VAT is calculated as an inclusive tax (the invoice total already includes VAT). The net amount and VAT amount are displayed separately on the invoice PDF.

> VAT is only applied when the VAT feature is enabled. The VAT settings require a VAT number and a membership VAT rate; <%= activities_human_name.downcase %> and shop VAT rates are optional and only used when those features are enabled.
<% end %>

## Payments {#payments}

Whenever a payment or invoice is created, or an invoice is canceled, the system distributes payments to existing invoices in this priority order:

1. Payment with reference number, redistribution until the referenced invoice is closed.
2. Redistribution of payments without reference number and excess amounts to invoices that were previously already marked as closed in chronological order.
3. Redistribution of payments without reference number and excess amounts to still open invoices in chronological order, the oldest invoices are closed first.

This redistribution mode is very convenient and thus allows managing cases where a member would reuse an old reference number to pay a new invoice.

### Automatic import {#automatic_payments_processing}

The most efficient way to process your payments is to ask your bank to set up [an EBICS 3.0 connection](https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/standardization.html#scrollTo=ebics). CSA Admin supports EBICS 3.0 (H005/BTF) only. Older EBICS 2.x (H003/H004) connections are not supported. The system can then import your members' payments each night from ISO camt.053/camt.054 files.

The bank form and the steps in CSA Admin are in [Setting up EBICS](#ebics-setup).

> If you have questions about a particular bank, [ask me](/support).

### Setting up EBICS {#ebics-setup}

An EBICS 3.0 (H005/BTF) connection lets CSA Admin fetch your members' payments every night. Setup usually takes a few days, because the bank validates a signed initialization letter before the connection can be used. You fill in the bank form and enter the identifiers yourself in [Bank connection settings](/settings#bank_connection).

1. [Fill in the bank form](#ebics-bank-form).
2. [Enter the identifiers](#ebics-in-app) and click **Start EBICS setup**.
3. [Sign the initialization letter](#ebics-letter), each page, and send it to the bank.
4. The bank validates the letter. CSA Admin checks once a day and [activates the connection](#ebics-letter).

Until then, use [manual import](#manual-import). EBICS is separate from e-banking access. The connection only fetches what the contract with the bank allows.

#### The bank form {#ebics-bank-form}

Tell the bank you want EBICS 3.0 (H005/BTF), so accounting software can fetch the payment files every night.

On the software lines of the form, write:

- Vendor / manufacturer: `CSA Admin (Thibaud Guillaume-Gentil)`
- Product, including version: `CSA Admin, EBICS 3.0 (H005)`

<!-- country:CH -->
Ask for:

- a daily QR payment report and a credit advice, both in **camt.054** (CSA Admin fetches this file each night)

Any camt version is fine: 2009/04 or 2019/08. A form may also say 2013, which is the same family as 2009/04. If the form allows more than one version, requesting both is fine. One version is enough for CSA Admin.

Do not request payment orders, LSV / Swiss direct debit, intraday movements (camt.052), or PDF documents.

The bank's distributed electronic signature lets several people approve payment orders. Forms sometimes call it SED or VEU. This connection only retrieves statements. Leave that option empty, or answer no.
<!-- /country:CH -->

<!-- country:DE -->
Ask for a daily end-of-day account statement in **camt.053**. CSA Admin fetches this file each night.

Any camt version is fine: 2009/04 or 2019/08. A form may also say 2013, which is the same family as 2009/04. If the form allows more than one version, requesting both is fine. One version is enough for CSA Admin.

If SEPA direct debit is used and a creditor identifier is set in [the SEPA settings](/settings#sepa), also ask the bank to allow a **pain.008** upload. That upload includes a technical signature. It is not the bank's distributed electronic signature, where several people approve each payment (sometimes called SED or VEU). Leave that bank option off.

Do not request payment orders, intraday movements (camt.052), or PDF documents.
<!-- /country:DE -->

In the account section of the form, enter the account IBAN.

> EBICS is not necessarily free at every bank. Ask your bank about its conditions.

#### Identifiers the bank sends back {#ebics-identifiers}

Once the bank has processed the contract, it sends four values. They usually arrive on a parameter sheet for the EBICS contract:

- **EBICS URL**. If the bank gives the host and the path separately, join them into one https address and keep the path, for example `https://ebics.example.ch/ebics.aspx`.
- **Host ID**
- **Client/Contract/Partner ID**. The bank may call this Client ID, Contract ID, Partner ID, or Customer ID.
- **Participant/User ID**. The bank may call this Participant ID, User ID, or Subscriber ID.

#### Enter them in CSA Admin {#ebics-in-app}

Open [Bank connection settings](/settings#bank_connection) and click **Start EBICS setup**. Enter the four values under **EBICS contract identifiers**. Tick **I confirm that these identifiers come from the bank EBICS contract.** and click **Start**.

CSA Admin checks the URL first. The address must be https, with no user or password in it, and the bank must answer as an EBICS 3.0 endpoint, path included. It then checks the Host ID, then the client and participant identifiers. If one value is rejected, compare it with the parameter sheet. If the values match the contract and the error remains, [contact me](/support).

**Start** prepares the initialization letter.

#### Initialization letter {#ebics-letter}

Click **Download initialization letter**. Banks often call this the INI letter. Each page has its own signature block: the signature key, the authentication key, and the encryption key. Sign **each page** and send the letter to the bank promptly. A letter that sits too long can leave the access inactive, or the initialization can go stale.

The bank often needs a few days to validate the letter. The connection stays on **Waiting for bank**. CSA Admin checks once a day. When the bank has accepted the letter, that check activates the connection.

If it stays on **Waiting for bank**, ask the bank whether the signed letter was processed. If it was, and the connection is still inactive, [contact me](/support).

#### Until the connection is active {#ebics-meanwhile}

Use [manual import](#manual-import) for payments that arrive before go-live, and for any earlier payments you still need to record. Do that while **"Manual Import"** is still on the payments page. That section is hidden once the connection is active, and CSA Admin then fetches new files each night. If the connection is already active and older payments are missing, [contact me](/support).

Payments with no reference number are still entered by hand.

On the ["Invoice overdue notice" email](/mail_templates/invoice_overdue_notice), leave **Send** unchecked until those earlier payments are imported. Notices go out only when automatic import is active and **Send** is checked. See [Overdue notice](#overdue_notice). Leaving **Send** off until the import is done avoids reminding members who have already paid.

<!-- country:CH -->
You can enter the [QR-IBAN](#qr-iban) in [the invoice settings](/settings#invoice) before EBICS is ready, and start invoicing. If you are moving from an old account to a new one, new invoices use the new QR-IBAN. Payments that still arrive on the old account have to be imported manually until those invoices are closed. Invoicing on the new account and that import can run at the same time, while the EBICS connection is not yet active.
<!-- /country:CH -->

<!-- country:!CH -->
You can enter the IBAN in [the invoice settings](/settings#invoice) before EBICS is ready, and start invoicing. If you are moving from an old account to a new one, new invoices use the new IBAN. Payments that still arrive on the old account have to be imported manually until those invoices are closed. Both can run at the same time, while the EBICS connection is not yet active.
<!-- /country:!CH -->

### Manual import {#manual-import}

When automatic import via [EBICS](https://www.six-group.com/en/products-services/banking-services/standardization.html#scrollTo=ebics) is not active yet, download a camt.053, camt.054, or mt940 file from your e-banking and upload it from [the payments page](/payments), section **"Manual Import"** in the right column. Repeat this about once a week until EBICS is active. The section is hidden once the connection is active.

<!-- country:CH -->
For QR invoices, prefer camt.054, or a camt.053 that still contains each QR reference. A highly aggregated camt.053 statement can list amounts and leave out the references, so the invoices stay open.
<!-- /country:CH -->

<!-- country:DE -->
Prefer an end-of-day camt.053. That is the file EBICS fetches once the connection is active.
<!-- /country:DE -->

For payments without a reference number, such as cash or a transfer that does not include one, [create a payment manually](/payments/new). Its amount is redistributed to open invoices.

> Stick to a single format. Using more than one can create the same payment twice.

### Refund {#refund}

An overpayment leaves a **positive balance** on the member. The next invoice absorbs it. A refund is a [negative payment](/payments/new), not a negative invoice. CSA Admin cannot send the bank transfer: do that from your e-banking.

