## Overdue notice {#overdue_notice}

<% overdue_notice_days = MailTemplate.delay_in_days_for("invoice_overdue_notice") %>
When payments are imported automatically, the system sends a reminder to every member with an unpaid invoice every <%= overdue_notice_days %> days after the invoice is sent, then again after the last notice, until it is paid (1st reminder after <%= overdue_notice_days %> days, 2nd after <%= overdue_notice_days * 2 %> days, and so on). SEPA invoices are not reminded. The delay and the text are set on [the "Invoice overdue notice" email](/mail_templates/invoice_overdue_notice).

> You can be notified by email when the 3rd reminder of an invoice is sent. Manage your notifications from [your admin account](/admins/<%= current_admin.id %>/edit).

## Admin notifications {#notifications}

Several billing-related events can trigger email notifications to administrators who have opted in via [their notification preferences](/admins/<%= current_admin.id %>/edit):

- **Invoice overpaid**: Sent when payments attached to an invoice exceed its amount, often because a previous QR reference was reused. Surplus is applied to the member's other invoices, or kept as a positive balance. The member's balance may already be zero.
- **3rd overdue notice**: Sent when the third reminder is sent for an unpaid invoice, signaling a persistent payment issue.
- **Payment reversal**: Sent when a negative payment (reversal) is imported, which may indicate a chargeback or bank correction.
